Where the animation styles come from
------------------------------------

Basic & Piano
  Fully original work by Anasentrik, ported from Anasentrik's own Python generators (MMA_Standar_FINAL.py,
  Real_Piano_StainedGlass_FINALv6.py).
  piano-visualizer-mcversion-26.3, Copyright (C) 2026 Anasentrik, GPL-3.0-or-later
  https://github.com/anasentrik/piano-visualizer-mcversion-26.3

Fretboard
  Fully original work by Anasentrik, written directly in this mod (no earlier Python generator): fretboard layout,
  auto-fingering, string lighting / vibration / bend, bodies, depth, and the readers for TAB from MusicXML, MuseScore
  files, per-string MIDI and PDF (PdfRaw.java, PdfTab.java, own PDF reader, no third-party library).
  The PDF reader uses the code points of SMuFL (Standard Music Font Layout, W3C Music Notation Community Group,
  https://www.w3.org/2021/03/smufl14/) to recognise music symbols. It was tested against the PDMX dataset (P. Long,
  Z. Novack, T. Berg-Kirkpatrick, J. McAuley, "PDMX: A Large-Scale Public Domain MusicXML Dataset for Symbolic Music
  Processing", https://zenodo.org/records/15571083); no file from PDMX is included in this program.
  Body outlines & patterns from 3D models: see "Fretboard bodies made from 3D models" below.

Bounce
  Based on Bouncing Playground, Copyright (C) 2026 Anasentrik, GPL-3.0-or-later
  https://github.com/anasentrik/bouncing-playground
  Bouncing Playground is a heavily modified version of midi-playground by Anasentrik, who wrote or changed the
  physics, motion modes, effects, 3D depth, menus and settings, the clip timeline editor, sheet music / audio / video
  input, and recording.
  midi-playground, Copyright (C) quasar098 and the original contributors, GPL-3.0
  https://github.com/quasar098/midi-playground
  Contributors: quasar098, TheCodingCrafter, PurpleJuiceBox, sled45, Times0, Spring-Forever-with-me, sj-dan,
  cangerjun, lucmsilva651, leo539, simpansoftware, slideglide, Guavvva, zetlen, SpeckyYT, suzuuuuu09

Hop & Sheet Music Bounce
  Concept from AMV (Automatic Melody Visualizer), a Blender add-on by Patrick / Polyfjord, GPL-3.0-or-later
  https://tools.polyfjord.com  -  https://www.youtube.com/@Polyfjord
  Rewritten in Java for Minecraft. The notation engine (key, spelling, beams, ties, staves) is new and follows the
  rules of standard music notation instead of AMV's duration-based symbols.

Spectrum Orbit
  Concept and analysis approach from Metriq Visualizer, Copyright (c) 2026 Metriq Foundation, Inc., MPL-2.0
  https://github.com/MetriqOrg/Metriq-Visualizer
  The audio feature and point-cloud code (AudioFeatures.java, OrbitGeometry.java, PreviewOrbit.java) follows the
  Metriq approach. To the extent any of it is derived from Metriq's source, those parts stay under the Mozilla Public
  License 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/), which allows them to be combined with this GPL-3.0 program.
  This project is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Metriq Foundation. "Metriq" is their trademark;
  it is used here only to name the origin of the concept.


Logo, icon and Sampler
----------------------

The MAG logo and icon are original work by Anasentrik. Copyright (C) 2026 Anasentrik. All rights reserved.
  Files: src/main/resources/assets/musicanim/icon.png and src/main/resources/assets/musicanim/textures/gui/mark_*.png
