  use them, or anything confusingly similar, for any other project, product, or modified version (fork) without
  written permission from Anasentrik. A modified version must replace them with its own logo and icon and must not
  present itself as the official Music Animation Generator.

The Sampler detects root notes with the YIN algorithm (A. de Cheveigné and H. Kawahara, "YIN, a fundamental frequency
estimator for speech and music", J. Acoust. Soc. Am. 111(4), 2002), implemented from the paper. It only reads
Minecraft's own sound files at run time; no Minecraft or third-party sound file is included in this program.


Fretboard bodies made from 3D models
------------------------------------

These Fretboard bodies are front-view outlines (shape plus a dominant color), small front-view pattern images
(88 columns, 48 colors) and a front-view 3D relief (144 columns, color plus front / back depth per cell) taken from 3D
models published on Sketchfab under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The models themselves are not included; the outlines, patterns and
reliefs were extracted from a front render, straightened, simplified, downscaled, color-reduced, mirrored where needed
and turned into data (src/main/java/dev/musicanim/FretBodies.java and
src/main/resources/assets/musicanim/fretbody/*.png, *.mesh).
